{"lyrics":"[00:02.62]Empty out your pockets, I need all that\n[00:05.44]Yeah, yeah\n[00:06.46]G-Money said, \"We need all the money, man\"\n[00:09.10]Pennies and all that\n[00:15.22]With G-Money, if I don't care if he got a million in all pennies\n[00:17.52]I'ma be countin' Abe Lincolns all day\n[00:19.24]Yeah, yeah, uh\n[00:20.90]Empty out your pockets, I need all that\n[00:23.06]I get the millions, then I fall back\n[00:25.58]Niggas chameleons, they'll change for some change\n[00:28.46]The days ain't the same, niggas switch for the fame\n[00:31.10]Louis Vuitton, I'm in my bag\n[00:33.14]Get high, then my memory gone, I've been hurtin'\n[00:35.60]I rock like electric guitars, I be ragin'\n[00:38.72]Countin' big knots, look like yellow pages\n[00:41.08]I run it like a race\n[00:43.32]Get in the way, brodie got the aim\n[00:45.98]To blow you away, the next day, you in the newspaper, on the front page\n[00:49.48]Prayin' for forgiveness, 'cause it happened on a Sunday\n[00:52.12]Back to the cash, rack after rack, so many racks that I sag\n[00:55.76]I just bought a bike, catch me doin' wheelies in the backstreet\n[00:58.38]Like I'm from where Meek Mill be\n[00:59.58]Put the \"dead\" in dead serious, you try me, then you will be\n[01:02.28]On my wrist, it's a ICEE, no, it ain't melting\n[01:04.92]Turn my closet to a freezer, AP on the shelf (Gleam)\n[01:07.84]Everybody doubted me, they ain't give me no help (Please)\n[01:10.04]So all this money in my pocket, I'ma spend it by myself (Self)\n[01:13.56]I bet you never felt this pain I felt\n[01:16.10]When mom ain't had no money and them bills brought hell\n[01:18.84]That's when G-Money hit my cell\n[01:21.00]Next day, would've fucked up and ended up in a cell\n[01:25.44]Uh, oh, hell (Fucked up and ended up in a cell)\n[01:27.70]Ended up in a cell (In a cell)\n[01:31.02]Oh, hell\n[01:31.28]Yeah, yeah, uh (Ended up in a cell)\n[01:34.20]Empty out your pockets, I need all that\n[01:36.10]I get the millions, then I fall back\n[